      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] The commit message states that `std::ranges::copy` \"completely eliminat[es] the risk of ... potential buffer overflows\", but this is not entirely accurate. \n\nWhile `std::ranges::copy` safely determines the bound of the *source* range (`p-\u003euserid`), it does not perform any bounds checking on the *destination* iterator (`global_context.user_id.begin()`). \n\nIf `p-\u003euserid` were ever larger than `global_context.user_id`, this would result in a destination buffer overflow. In contrast, the original `memcpy` used `sizeof(global_context.user_id)`, which guaranteed the destination buffer would not be overflowed (though it risked over-reading the source).\n\nTo truly eliminate the risk of size mismatches and ensure safety, I highly recommend adding a `static_assert` to enforce that the sizes match exactly:\n\n```cpp\nstatic_assert(std::size(p-\u003euserid) \u003d\u003d std::size(global_context.user_id));\nstd::ranges::copy(p-\u003euserid, global_context.user_id.begin());\n```",
